  message: "From WI-sipuk (registry cross-reference sub-check, branch jgstern-agent/feat/sipuk-registry-refs, unmerged): that check does NOT cover this item's defect, so do not count on it to catch the next one of this shape. Probed directly: scripts/check-docstring-drift's registry_hits_in_source over scripts/generate_schema_lib.py returns zero hits. There are three reasons. (1) The drift here is a stale CLAIM: emit sites that no longer exist, and an enum held open \"until Phase 4b\" after Phase 4b shipped. No retired NAME is involved, and the check is name-exact. (2) kind=f\"ipc_{...}\" is a dynamic f-string, not a name. (3) The default scope is packages/*/src, and the generator is in scripts/. The tracker-refs and phase-markers sub-checks are the closer fit for the \"until ... Phase 4b ... land\" wording, but they share the packages/*/src default scope too. Pass scripts/ as a positional path to scan it."  # c800
